{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21526288",
      "title": "Module Summary",
      "lectureOrder": 126,
      "videoOrder": 109,
      "sourceHash": "9983a571ad01efe1997956eb683b6a9faaddeb4004a070a23ea3992236c59364",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.44,
          "end": 5.07,
          "en": "That was another long module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.07,
          "end": 6.54,
          "en": "about components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.54,
          "end": 8.8,
          "en": "But we're never done with components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.8,
          "end": 12.17,
          "en": "We now know all the core features you need to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.17,
          "end": 15.36,
          "en": "and in the next module, we are going to practice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.36,
          "end": 17.7,
          "en": "all the features we learned in this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.7,
          "end": 21.72,
          "en": "and the previous modules by building a complete project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.72,
          "end": 23.45,
          "en": "A complete app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.45,
          "end": 25.5,
          "en": "Now in this module, we had a look at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.5,
          "end": 28.32,
          "en": "component registration and styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.32,
          "end": 30.06,
          "en": "And you learned that components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.06,
          "end": 34.12,
          "en": "can be registered globally or locally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.12,
          "end": 37.01,
          "en": "Globally with the app component method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.01,
          "end": 39.56,
          "en": "locally by importing them and adding them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.56,
          "end": 42.88,
          "en": "to the components option in the conflict object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.88,
          "end": 45.04,
          "en": "of a component or app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.04,
          "end": 49.16,
          "en": "You should prefer local registration for most components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.16,
          "end": 51.48,
          "en": "But if you have components which you are using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.48,
          "end": 54.02,
          "en": "in a lot of different places off your app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.02,
          "end": 57.883,
          "en": "then of course global registration makes a lot of sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59,
          "end": 60.68,
          "en": "We also had a look at styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.68,
          "end": 64.58,
          "en": "and styling can also be global or scoped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.58,
          "end": 68.28,
          "en": "Global styles affect all HTML elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.28,
          "end": 70.81,
          "en": "no matter in which component they are.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.81,
          "end": 75.2,
          "en": "And scoped styles only affect the HTML elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.2,
          "end": 79.77,
          "en": "in the template off the component where you are using them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.77,
          "end": 83.56,
          "en": "You should prefer scoped styles for most components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.56,
          "end": 87.25,
          "en": "But definitely set up global application wide styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.25,
          "end": 91.37,
          "en": "like a font family in a unscoped style tag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.37,
          "end": 93.32300000000001,
          "en": "in your app.Vue file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.9,
          "end": 99.05,
          "en": "We also had a look at slots, another key feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.05,
          "end": 102.27000000000001,
          "en": "Slots can in the end be used as a placeholder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.27000000000001,
          "end": 104.28,
          "en": "for dynamic HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.28,
          "end": 109.03,
          "en": "which can then be inserted from outside into a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.03,
          "end": 110.93,
          "en": "You can have single slots.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.93,
          "end": 112.75999999999999,
          "en": "You can have multiple slots",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.75999999999999,
          "end": 115.21000000000001,
          "en": "where you then also need names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.21000000000001,
          "end": 118.68,
          "en": "Only one slot may stay unnamed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.68,
          "end": 122.39,
          "en": "You can provide default content for slots,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.39,
          "end": 124.47,
          "en": "which will be used as a fallback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.47,
          "end": 128.45,
          "en": "if no content is provided for that slot from outside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.45,
          "end": 130.96,
          "en": "And we learned about scope slots",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.96,
          "end": 133.323,
          "en": "for some advanced use cases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.68,
          "end": 137.28,
          "en": "Slots are another key feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.28,
          "end": 141.92000000000002,
          "en": "which unlock rapper components like cards or dialogs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.92000000000002,
          "end": 145.503,
          "en": "and you will see them in action again in the next module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.59,
          "end": 149.14,
          "en": "We also have dynamic components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.14,
          "end": 151.82,
          "en": "Dynamic components is a feature built in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.82,
          "end": 154.933,
          "en": "to view unlocked with the built-in component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.11,
          "end": 158.7,
          "en": "This can be used to dynamically swap it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.7,
          "end": 161.32,
          "en": "for different components you defined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.32,
          "end": 164.91,
          "en": "And you can also control the caching of that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.91,
          "end": 167.57,
          "en": "with the built-in keep alive component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.57,
          "end": 169.73,
          "en": "as you learned it in this module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.73,
          "end": 173.47,
          "en": "We will also use this feature in the next course module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 173.47,
          "end": 175.903,
          "en": "So, in the project we're going to build there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.29,
          "end": 180.12,
          "en": "Now last but not least, we have a look at teleport",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.12,
          "end": 182.3,
          "en": "and the official style guide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.3,
          "end": 186.78,
          "en": "Teleport is another built-in component which can be used to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.78,
          "end": 189.9,
          "en": "manipulate the DOM structure and control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.9,
          "end": 192.82,
          "en": "where something is added to the real DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.82,
          "end": 195.1,
          "en": "whilst keeping your component hierarchy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.1,
          "end": 197.603,
          "en": "So that will not be changed by teleport.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.039,
          "end": 199.872,
          "en": "And last but not least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 199.872,
          "end": 202.36,
          "en": "I introduced you to the official style guide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.36,
          "end": 205.03,
          "en": "And you might want to consider following that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.03,
          "end": 206.81,
          "en": "or at least have a look at it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 206.81,
          "end": 209.72,
          "en": "to keep your code clean and understandable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 209.72,
          "end": 211.46,
          "en": "And that's it for this module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.46,
          "end": 213.67000000000002,
          "en": "In the next module we're going to practice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 213.67000000000002,
          "end": 216.793,
          "en": "what we learned here and in the previous modules.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
